#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.44 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:5
msgid "Backward Compatibility Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:9
msgid ""
"\"git checkout -B <branch>\" used to allow switching to a branch that is in "
"use on another worktree, but this was by mistake.  The users need to use \"--"
"ignore-other-worktrees\" option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:12
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:15
msgid ""
"\"git add\" and \"git stash\" learned to support the \":(attr:...)\" magic "
"pathspec."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:18
msgid ""
"\"git rebase --autosquash\" is now enabled for non-interactive rebase, but "
"it is still incompatible with the apply backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:21
msgid ""
"Introduce \"git replay\", a tool meant on the server side without working "
"tree to recreate a history."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:24
msgid ""
"\"git merge-file\" learned to take the \"--diff-algorithm\" option to use "
"algorithm different from the default \"myers\" diff."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:28
msgid ""
"Command line completion (in contrib/) learned to complete path arguments to "
"the \"add/set\" subcommands of \"git sparse-checkout\" better."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:35
msgid ""
"\"git checkout -B <branch> [<start-point>]\" allowed a branch that is in use "
"in another worktree to be updated and checked out, which might be a bit "
"unexpected.  The rule has been tightened, which is a breaking change.  \"--"
"ignore-other-worktrees\" option is required to unbreak you, if you are used "
"to the current behaviour that \"-B\" overrides the safety."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:40
msgid ""
"The builtin_objectmode attribute is populated for each path without adding "
"anything in .gitattributes files, which would be useful in magic pathspec, e."
"g., \":(attr:builtin_objectmode=100755)\" to limit to executables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:44
msgid ""
"\"git fetch\" learned to pay attention to \"fetch.all\" configuration "
"variable, which pretends as if \"--all\" was passed from the command line "
"when no remote parameter was given."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:48
msgid ""
"In addition to (rather cryptic) Security Identifiers, show username and "
"domain in the error message when we barf on mismatch between the Git "
"directory and the current user on Windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:52
msgid ""
"The error message given when \"git branch -d branch\" fails due to commits "
"unique to the branch has been split into an error and a new conditional "
"advice message."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:56
msgid ""
"When given an existing but unreadable file as a configuration file, gitweb "
"behaved as if the file did not exist at all, but now it errors out.  This is "
"a change that may break backward compatibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:61
msgid ""
"When $HOME/.gitconfig is missing but XDG config file is available, we should "
"write into the latter, not former.  \"git gc\" and \"git maintenance\" wrote "
"into a wrong \"global config\" file, which have been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:65
msgid ""
"Define \"special ref\" as a very narrow set that consists of FETCH_HEAD and "
"MERGE_HEAD, and clarify everything else that used to be classified as such "
"are actually just pseudorefs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:69
msgid ""
"All conditional \"advice\" messages show how to turn them off, which becomes "
"repetitive.  Setting advice.* configuration explicitly on now omits the "
"instruction part."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:76
msgid ""
"The \"disable repository discovery of a bare repository\" check, triggered "
"by setting safe.bareRepository configuration variable to 'explicit', has "
"been loosened to exclude the \".git/\" directory inside a non-bare "
"repository from the check.  So you can do \"cd .git && git cmd\" to run a "
"Git command that works on a bare repository without explicitly specifying "
"$GIT_DIR now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:79
msgid ""
"The completion script (in contrib/) learned more options that can be used "
"with \"git log\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:83
msgid ""
"The labels on conflict markers for the common ancestor, our version, and the "
"other version are available to custom 3-way merge driver via %S, %X, and %Y "
"placeholders."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:86
msgid ""
"The write codepath for the reftable data learned to honor core.fsync "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:89
msgid ""
"The \"--fsck-objects\" option of \"git index-pack\" now can take the "
"optional parameter to tweak severity of different fsck errors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:93
msgid ""
"The wincred credential backend has been taught to support oauth refresh "
"token the same way as credential-cache and credential-libsecret backends."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:96
msgid ""
"Command line completion support (in contrib/) has been updated for \"git "
"bisect\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:101
msgid ""
"\"git branch\" and friends learned to use the formatted text as sorting key, "
"not the underlying timestamp value, when the --sort option is used with "
"author or committer timestamp with a format specifier (e.g., \"--"
"sort=creatordate:format:%H:%M:%S\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:104
msgid ""
"The command line completion script (in contrib/) learned to complete "
"configuration variable names better."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:107
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:109
msgid "Process to add some form of low-level unit tests has started."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:111
msgid "Add support for GitLab CI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:116
msgid ""
"\"git for-each-ref --no-sort\" still sorted the refs alphabetically which "
"paid non-trivial cost.  It has been redefined to show output in an "
"unspecified order, to allow certain optimizations to take advantage of."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:119
msgid ""
"Simplify API implementation to delete references by eliminating duplication."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:121
msgid "Subject approxidate() and show_date() machinery to OSS-Fuzz."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:124
msgid ""
"A new helper to let us pretend that we called lstat() when we know our "
"cache_entry is up-to-date via fsmonitor."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:127
msgid ""
"The optimization based on fsmonitor in the \"diff --cached\" codepath is "
"resurrected with the \"fake-lstat\" introduced earlier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:130
msgid "Test balloon to use C99 \"bool\" type from <stdbool.h> has been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:134
msgid ""
"\"git clone\" has been prepared to allow cloning a repository with non-"
"default hash function into a repository that uses the reftable backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:138
msgid ""
"Streaming spans of packfile data used to be done only from a single, "
"primary, pack in a repository with multiple packfiles.  It has been extended "
"to allow reuse from other packfiles, too."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:141
msgid ""
"Comment updates to help developers not to attempt to modify messages from "
"plumbing commands that must stay constant."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:144
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It might make sense to reassess the plumbing needs every few years,\n"
"but that should be done as a separate effort.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:146
msgid "Move test-ctype helper to the unit-test framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:150
msgid ""
"Instead of manually creating refs/ hierarchy on disk upon a creation of a "
"secondary worktree, which is only usable via the files backend, use the refs "
"API to populate it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:152
msgid "CI for GitLab learned to drive macOS jobs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:155
msgid ""
"A few tests to \"git commit -o <pathspec>\" and \"git commit -i <pathspec>\" "
"has been added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:157
msgid "Tests on ref API are moved around to prepare for reftable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:161
msgid ""
"The Makefile often had to say \"-L$(path) -R$(path)\" that repeats the path "
"to the same library directory for link time and runtime.  A Makefile "
"template is used to reduce such repetition."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:164
msgid ""
"The priority queue test has been migrated to the unit testing framework."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:167
msgid ""
"Setting `feature.experimental` opts the user into multi-pack reuse experiment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:171
msgid ""
"Squelch node.js 16 deprecation warnings from GitHub Actions CI by updating "
"actions/github-script and actions/checkout that use node.js 20."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:176
msgid ""
"The mechanism to report the filename in the source code, used by the unit-"
"test machinery, assumed that the compiler expanded __FILE__ to the path to "
"the source given to the $(CC), but some compilers give full path, breaking "
"the output.  This has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:179
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.43"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:183
msgid ""
"The way CI testing used \"prove\" could lead to running the test suite twice "
"needlessly, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:185
msgid "Update ref-related tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:188
msgid ""
"\"git format-patch --encode-email-headers\" ignored the option when "
"preparing the cover letter, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:193
msgid ""
"Newer versions of Getopt::Long started giving warnings against our (ab)use "
"of it in \"git send-email\".  Bump the minimum version requirement for Perl "
"to 5.8.1 (from September 2002) to allow simplifying our implementation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:198
msgid ""
"Earlier we stopped relying on commit-graph that (still) records information "
"about commits that are lost from the object store, which has negative "
"performance implications.  The default has been flipped to disable this "
"pessimization."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:201
msgid ""
"Stale URLs have been updated to their current counterparts (or archive.org) "
"and HTTP links are replaced with working HTTPS links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:204
msgid ""
"trace2 streams used to record the URLs that potentially embed authentication "
"material, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:209
msgid ""
"The sample pre-commit hook that tries to catch introduction of new paths "
"that use potentially non-portable characters did not notice an existing path "
"getting renamed to such a problematic path, when rename detection was "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:214
msgid ""
"The command line parser for the \"log\" family of commands was too loose "
"when parsing certain numbers, e.g., silently ignoring the extra 'q' in \"git "
"log -n 1q\" without complaining, which has been tightened up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:218
msgid ""
"\"git $cmd --end-of-options --rev -- --path\" for some $cmd failed to "
"interpret \"--rev\" as a rev, and \"--path\" as a path.  This was fixed for "
"many programs like \"reset\" and \"checkout\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:221
msgid ""
"\"git bisect reset\" has been taught to clean up state files and refs even "
"when BISECT_START file is gone."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:224
msgid ""
"Some codepaths did not correctly parse configuration variables specified "
"with valueless \"true\", which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:227
msgid ""
"Code clean-up for sanity checking of command line options for \"git show-"
"ref\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:230
msgid ""
"The code to parse the From e-mail header has been updated to avoid recursion."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:233
msgid ""
"\"git fetch --atomic\" issued an unnecessary empty error message, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:236
msgid ""
"Command line completion script (in contrib/) learned to work better with the "
"reftable backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:239
msgid ""
"\"git status\" is taught to show both the branch being bisected and being "
"rebased when both are in effect at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:242
msgid ""
"\"git archive --list extra garbage\" silently ignored excess command line "
"parameters, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:246
msgid ""
"\"git sparse-checkout set\" added default patterns even when the patterns "
"are being fed from the standard input, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:249
msgid ""
"\"git sparse-checkout (add|set) --[no-]cone --end-of-options\" did not "
"handle \"--end-of-options\" correctly after a recent update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:253
msgid ""
"Unlike other environment variables that took the usual true/false/yes/no as "
"well as 0/1, GIT_FLUSH only understood 0/1, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:258
msgid ""
"Clearing in-core repository (happens during e.g., \"git fetch --recurse-"
"submodules\" with commit graph enabled) made in-core commit object in an "
"inconsistent state by discarding the necessary data from commit-graph too "
"early, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:260
msgid "Update to a new feature recently added, \"git show-ref --exists\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:263
msgid ""
"oss-fuzz tests are built and run in CI.  (merge c4a9cf1df3 js/oss-fuzz-build-"
"in-ci later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:266
msgid ""
"Rename detection logic ignored the final line of a file if it is an "
"incomplete line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:269
msgid ""
"GitHub CI update.  (merge 0188b2c8e0 pb/ci-github-skip-logs-for-broken-tests "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:272
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-rename A B\" did not disable rename detection but did not "
"trigger an error from the command line parser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:276
msgid ""
"\"git archive --remote=<remote>\" learned to talk over the smart http (aka "
"stateless) transport.  (merge 176cd68634 jx/remote-archive-over-smart-http "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:280
msgid ""
"Fetching via protocol v0 over Smart HTTP transport sometimes failed to "
"correctly auto-follow tags.  (merge fba732c462 jk/fetch-auto-tag-following-"
"fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:285
msgid ""
"The documentation for the --exclude-per-directory option marked it as "
"deprecated, which confused readers into thinking there may be a plan to "
"remove it in the future, which was not our intention.  (merge 0009542cab jc/"
"ls-files-doc-update later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:288
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-index file1 file2\" segfaulted while invoking the external "
"diff driver, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:291
msgid ""
"Rewrite //-comments to /* comments */ in files whose comments prevalently "
"use the latter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:295
msgid ""
"Cirrus CI jobs started breaking because we specified version of FreeBSD that "
"is no longer available, which has been corrected.  (merge 81fffb66d3 cb/use-"
"freebsd-13-2-at-cirrus-ci later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:299
msgid ""
"A caller called index_file_exists() that takes a string expressed as <ptr, "
"length> with a wrong length, which has been corrected.  (merge 156e28b36d jh/"
"sparse-index-expand-to-path-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:302
msgid ""
"A failed \"git tag -s\" did not necessarily result in an error depending on "
"the crypto backend, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:305
msgid ""
"\"git stash\" sometimes was silent even when it failed due to unwritable "
"index file, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:308
msgid ""
"\"git show-ref --verify\" did not show things like \"CHERRY_PICK_HEAD\", "
"which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:312
msgid ""
"Recent conversion to allow more than 0/1 in GIT_FLUSH broke the mechanism by "
"flipping what yes/no means by mistake, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:319
msgid ""
"The sequencer machinery does not use the ref API and instead records names "
"of certain objects it needs for its correct operation in temporary files, "
"which makes these objects susceptible to loss by garbage collection.  These "
"temporary files have been added as starting points for reachability analysis "
"to fix this.  (merge bc7f5db896 pw/gc-during-rebase later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:323
msgid ""
"\"git cherry-pick\" invoked during \"git rebase -i\" session lost the "
"authorship information, which has been corrected.  (merge e4301f73ff vn/"
"rebase-with-cherry-pick-authorship later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:327
msgid ""
"The code paths that call repo_read_object_file() have been tightened to "
"react to errors.  (merge 568459bf5e js/check-null-from-read-object-file "
"later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/RelNotes/2.44.0.txt:334
msgid ""
"Other code cleanup, docfix, build fix, etc.  (merge 5aea3955bc rj/clarify-"
"branch-doc-m later to maint).  (merge 9cce3be2df bk/bisect-doc-fix later to "
"maint).  (merge 8430b438f6 vd/fsck-submodule-url-test later to maint).  "
"(merge 3cb4384683 jc/t0091-with-unknown-git later to maint).  (merge "
"020456cb74 rs/receive-pack-remove-find-header later to maint).  (merge "
"bc47139f4f la/trailer-cleanups later to maint)."
msgstr ""
